<title>SENEGAL: Senegal phosphate company lays off most workers.</title>
<headline>Senegal phosphate company lays off most workers.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal's state-owned Societe Senegalaise des Phosphates de Thies (SSPT) said on Tuesday it had laid off most of its workers after a three-week pay strike.</p>
<p>&quot;We have layed off 140 people in a total of 154 workers,&quot; a senior manager at SSPT told Reuters. &quot;It is unacceptable to be on strike for such a long period.&quot;</p>
<p>Workers at the company, which is earmarked for privatisation, went on strike on April 7 seeking a 25 percent pay rise. Management had offered a 2.8 percent rise.</p>
<p>The state has a 50 percent stake in the capital of the company, which last year produced 64,000 tonnes of phosphate.</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
